      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَجْدَجٌ</span></b>  <i>It</i> (the night, S, and so in
some copies of the K) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, dark;</i>
(S, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَدَجْدَجَ</span></b>  (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَجْدَجَتِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الدَّجَاجَةُ فِى مَشْيِهَا</span> <i>The domestic fowl ran.</i> (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَجْدَجَ بِالدَّجَاجَةِ</span> <i>He called the cock,</i> or <i>hen,</i>
(S, K,) <i>by the cry</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَجْ دَجْ</span>, (K,) or, as in some
copies of the K [and in the L] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِجْ دِجْ</span>. (TA.)

